<title>USA: Cistron Q2 Dec 31 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Cistron Q2 Dec 31 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>PINE BROOK, N.J. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended December 31</p>
<p>							 1996	   1995</p>
<p> Net Sales				     $126,805	$134,170</p>
<p> Net Income (loss)			 12,140,163     (310,642)</p>
<p> Net Income (loss) per share - primary	.45	   (.01)</p>
<p>Net Income (loss) per share - fully diluted</p>
<p>							  .42		--</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding - primary		  26,884,990    26,882,990</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding fully diluted	    29,252,100		--</p>
<p>					   Six months ended December 31</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p> Net Sales					302,285	$268,004</p>
<p> Net Income (loss)			 11,899,024   (3,950,382)</p>
<p> Net Income (loss) per share - primary	.44	   (.01)</p>
<p>Net Income (loss) per share - fully diluted</p>
<p>							  .41		--</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  outstanding - primary		  26,884,133    26,882,990</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding - fully diluted	  29,251,243		--</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income and earnings per share for the second quarter and six months of 1996 were attributable mostly to a $21 million settlement of litigation to be paid to Cistron by Immunex Corp, which is a subsidiary of American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>The company also established a tax reserve of $2,573,000 as of December 31, 1996 and had net operating loss carryforwards of $8,956,000 and investment and research and development tax credits of $372,000.</p>
